          %h3#characterization_in_terms_of_dirac_structures Characterization in terms of Dirac structures
          %p
            D-branes may be identified with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+structures"} Dirac structures
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Courant+Lie+2-algebroid"} Courant Lie 2-algebroid
            over spacetime related to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+geometry"} type II geometry
            (
            %a{:href => "#AsakawaSasaWatamura"}> Asakawa-Sasa-Watamura
            ). See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+structure"} Dirac structure
            for more on this.
          %h3#DBraneCharge D-brane charge
          %p
            In analogy to how in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetism"} electromagnetism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+charge"} magnetic charge
            is given by a class in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+bundle"} Chan-Paton bundle
            carried by a D-brane defines a class in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            on the D-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            and the D-brane charge is the push-forward (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Umkehr+map"}> Umkehr map
            ) of this class to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-orientation"} K-orientation
            of the embedding of the D-brane (a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+structure"} spin^c structure
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+D-brane+charge"} K-theory classification of D-brane charge
          %h4#general General
          %p
            More in detail this means the following (
            %a{:href => "#BMRS2"}> BMRS2
            ).
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a manifold regarded as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Q
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon Q \hookrightarrow X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifold"} submanifold
            regarded as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            of a D-brane. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∇
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_B \colon X \to \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)_{conn}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-bundle+with+connection"} circle 2-bundle with connection
            which models the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_B \colon X \to \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
            for the underlying
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-group"} circle 2-group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+bundle"} Chan-Paton bundle
            (a
