                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+infinity-groupoid"} symplectic n-groupoid
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-plectic+geometry"} (n+1)-plectic geometry
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math#mathml_0477fc87f3bab6c93955b29dd7c515f68e3108fd_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo =
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = n+1
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AKSZ+sigma-model"} AKSZ sigma-model
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
            %p
              (adapted from
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Some+title+containing+the+words+%22homotopy%22+and+%22symplectic%22%2C+e.g.+this+one"} Ševera 00
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general_2 General
          %p The original article is
          %ul
            %li#Polchinski95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Polchinski"}> Joseph Polchinski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dirichlet-Branes and Ramond-Ramond Charges
                %strong 75
                (1995) 4724-4727 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9510017"}> arXiv:hep-th/9510017
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.75.4724"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.75.4724
              %p from p.7:
          %blockquote
            %p
              although it appears that we have modified the type II theory by adding something new to it, we are now arguing that these objects are actually intrinsic to any nonperturbative formulation of the type II theory; presumably one should think of them as an alternate representation of the black
              = succeed "-branes" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p General review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Polchinski"}> Joseph Polchinski
                ,
                %em TASI Lectures on D-Branes
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9611050"}> arXiv:hep-th/9611050
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Johnson98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+Johnson"}> Clifford Johnson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Études on D-Branes
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"} Mike Duff
                et. al. (eds.)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Nonperturbative aspects of strings, branes and supersymmetry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9812196"} arXiv:hep-th/9812196
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/481393"} spire:481393
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Koji+Hashimoto"}> Koji Hashimoto
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em D-Brane – Superstrings and New Perspective of Our World
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2F978-3-642-23574-0"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-23574-0
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/1188897"} spire:1188897
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fre"}> Pietro Fre
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Branes: Three Viewpoints
                %em Gravity, a Geometrical Course
                Springer 2013 (
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/1242195"}> spire:1242195
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-94-007-5443-0_7"} doi:10.1007/978-94-007-5443-0_7
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Bachas"}> Constantin Bachas
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em D-branes
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Quantum+Gravity"} Handbook of Quantum Gravity
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.18456"} arXiv:2311.18456
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-981-19-3079-9"} doi:10.1007/978-981-19-3079-9
          %p A classical text describing how the physics way to think of D-branes leads to seeing that they are objects in derived categories is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Aspinwall"}> Paul Aspinwall
              ,
              %em D-Branes on Calabi-Yau Manifolds
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0403166"}> arXiv:hep-th/0403166
              )
          %p
            Discussion with an eye towards
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            is in
          %ul
            %li#IbanezUranga12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luis+Ib%C3%A1%C3%B1ez"}> Luis Ibáñez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Angel+Uranga"} Angel Uranga
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+Theory+and+Particle+Physics+--+An+Introduction+to+String+Phenomenology"} String Theory and Particle Physics – An Introduction to String Phenomenology
          %p
            This can to a large extent be read as a dictionary from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            terminology to that of D-brane physics.
          %p
            More recent similar material with the emphasis on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            aspects is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"}> Richard Szabo
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Szabo09.pdf", :title => "D-Branes and Bivariant K-Theory"} D-Branes and Bivariant K-Theory
          %p
            Comments on the role of D-branes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"}> Gregory Moore
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Impact+of+D-Branes+on+Mathematics"} The Impact of D-Branes on Mathematics
              (2014)
          %h3#on_orbifolds On orbifolds
          %p Review includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Frederik Roose,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Strings and D-branes on orbifolds: from boundary states to geometry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://fys.kuleuven.be/itf/groups/hep/files/phd/fredrroose.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Nikolas Prezas,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Aspects of branes and orbifolds in string theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://dspace.mit.edu/bitstream/handle/1721.1/8486/50759455-MIT.pdf?sequence=2"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://hdl.handle.net/1721.1/8486"} web
          %p
            See also the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
          %h3#ReferencesAsGSsigmaModels
            As higher super-GS-WZW type
            = succeed "-models" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+model"} Green-Schwarz sigma model
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DBI+action"} DBI action
            for D-branes is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#CGNSW97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Cederwall"}> Martin Cederwall
                , Alexander von Gussich,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bengt+Nilsson"} Bengt Nilsson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Dirichlet Super-p-Branes in Ten-Dimensional Type IIA and IIB Supergravity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9611159"} arXiv:hep-th/9611159
            %li#APPS97b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mina+Aganagic"}> Mina Aganagic
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jaemo+Park"} Jaemo Park
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dual D-Brane Actions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9702133"} arXiv:hep-th/9702133
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functionals"} Green-Schwarz action functionals
            for super D-branes and the interpretation of the WZW cocycles for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            as cocycles on “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super-Minkowski+spacetime"}> extended super-Minkowski spacetime
            ” is due to
          %ul
            %li#CAIB99
              %p
                C. Chrysso‌malakos,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"} José de Azcárraga
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+M.+Izquierdo"} José M. Izquierdo
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The geometry of branes and extended superspaces
                %strong 567
                (2000) 293-330 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9904137"}> arXiv:hep-th/9904137
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213(99)00512-X"} doi:10.1016/S0550-3213(99)00512-X
            %li#Sakaguchi00
              %p
                Makoto Sakaguchi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em IIB-Branes and New Spacetime Superalgebras
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9909143"} arXiv:hep-th/9909143
            %li#AzcarragaIzquierdo01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"}> José de Azcárraga
                , J. M. Izquierdo,
                %em Superalgebra cohomology, the geometry of extended superspaces and superbranes
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0105125"}> arXiv:hep-th/0105125
                )
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+algebras+and+supersymmetry"} division algebras and supersymmetry
          %p
            A corresponding discussion as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} ∞-Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
            and refinement of the brane scan to a “brane bouquet” of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} super L-∞ algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} extensions
            (hence in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+theory"} infinity-Lie theory
            via
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} ∞-Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
          %ul
            %li#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.5264"} arXiv:1308.5264
            %li#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+WZW+term+of+the+M5-brane+and+differential+cohomotopy"} The WZW term of the M5-brane and differential cohomotopy
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1506.07557"} arXiv:1506.07557
            %li#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Rational+sphere+valued+supercocycles+in+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} Rational sphere valued supercocycles in M-theory and type IIA string theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03206"}> arXiv:1606.03206
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vincent+Braunack-Mayer"}> Vincent Braunack-Mayer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Gauge+enhancement+of+Super+M-Branes"} Gauge enhancement of Super M-Branes
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.01115"}> arXiv:1806.01115
                )
          %div
            %h3#DBraneChargeQuantizationInTopologicalKTheory D-brane charge quantization in topological K-theory
            %p
              On the conjectural
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge+quantization+in+topological+K-theory"} D-brane charge quantization in topological K-theory
            %h4#origin_and_basics Origin and basics
            %p
              The idea that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
              have
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              originates with the observation that their charge expressed in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+densities"} flux densities
              resembles the image of a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            %ul
              %li#GreenHarveyMoore97
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"}> Michael Green
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+A.+Harvey"} Jeffrey A. Harvey
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em I-Brane Inflow and Anomalous Couplings on D-Branes
                  %strong 14
                  (1997) 47-52
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9605033"} arXiv:hep-th/9605033
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/0264-9381/14/1/008"} doi:10.1088/0264-9381/14/1/008
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li#MinasianMoore97
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ruben+Minasian"}> Ruben Minasian
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em K-theory and Ramond-Ramond charge
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9710230"} arXiv:hep-th/9710230
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1126-6708/1997/11/002"} doi:10.1088/1126-6708/1997/11/002
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p Further early discussion:
            %ul
              %li#Witten98
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em D-Branes And K-Theory
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9810188"} arXiv:hep-th/9810188
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1126-6708/1998/12/019"} doi:10.1088/1126-6708/1998/12/019
              %li#Horava98
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Petr+Ho%C5%99ava"}> Petr Hořava
                  ,
                  %em Type IIA D-Branes, K-Theory, and Matrix Theory
                  (1998). (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9812135"}> hep-th/9812135
                  ).
              %li#FreedHopkins00
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em On Ramond-Ramond fields and K-theory
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0002027"} arXiv:hep-th/0002027
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1126-6708/2000/05/044"} doi:10.1088/1126-6708/2000/05/044
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              and with emphasis on the full picture of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+K-theory"} twisted
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
              in:
            %ul
              %li#Freed00
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization+and+generalized+differential+cohomology"} Dirac charge quantization and generalized differential cohomology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0011220"} arXiv:hep-th/0011220
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/SDG.2002.v7.n1.a6"} doi:10.4310/SDG.2002.v7.n1.a6
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/537392"} spire:537392
            %p#BasisOfTheConjecture Here:
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#GreenHarveyMoore97"}> Green, Harvey &amp; Moore (1997)
                ,
                %a{:href => "#MinasianMoore97"} Minasian &amp; Moore (1997)
                observe that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
                = succeed "-expressions" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} form
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
                look like images of K-theory classes under the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
              %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
                %img{:src => "/nlab/files/AntiBraneAnnihilationAsKGroupEquivRelation.jpg", :width => "300px"}/
                %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                  From
                  %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Equivariant+Stable+Cohomotopy+and+Branes"} Sch 18
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Witten98"} Witten 98, Section 3
                adds the observation that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tachyon+condensation"} tachyon condensation
                – which is expected (this is
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sen%27s+conjecture"} Sen's conjecture
                from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "Sen's+conjecture#ReferencesForSuperstrings"} Sen 98
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+strings"} open strings
                between
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-D-branes"} anti-D-branes
                – plausibly implements on their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+field"} Chan-Paton
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
                the defining
